{"id": "EUVD-2026-80444", "enisaUuid": "49aa7056-9fb6-3c7e-ad8d-464222ff3329", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Hold vport_slock for host map update in report ID acquisition\n\nqla24xx_report_id_acquisition() format-1 handling drops vport_slock after\ntaking the vport reference and then calls qla_update_host_map() without\nthe lock. That reaches qla_update_vp_map(), which mutates the ha->host_map\nbtree via btree_insert32()/btree_update32()/btree_remove32() and is\ndocumented to require vport_slock to be held by the caller. Running it\nunlocked can race concurrent host_map updates and corrupt the btree.\n\nThe format-2 path in the same function already wraps its host_map update\n(SET_AL_PA) in vport_slock; the format-1 path is the lone outlier.\n\nHold vport_slock across the format-1 qla_update_host_map() call to honor\nthe documented locking contract. The vref_count taken in the loop keeps\nthe vport valid, so this only adds the missing host_map serialization.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:37", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8f1b0cb9782338c6341ceed816e9c1243743cdd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ed66e2a67bbd22877008ff9aa64bd574a7fc011", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/776e4e8cbcf155302f430ce9793d1502e3c113a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d0b3f745efb24c0aac5e06b49b3420bc65d23b9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7944039ba9cb5c3a935d17c91004e3b8649ff58e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8hj3-p94r-f47v", "CVE-2026-89844"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11caa1a7-072a-3801-af4e-a733d0c23cf0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "23e2ce33-b970-35ff-ac28-2bc96592eb45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "430eef03a763e5e76a371ba6d02779ae4a64b6ea <6ed66e2a67bbd22877008ff9aa64bd574a7fc011"}, {"id": "25632f37-2d01-3b6a-bee9-d194bfadfb5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "430eef03a763e5e76a371ba6d02779ae4a64b6ea <7944039ba9cb5c3a935d17c91004e3b8649ff58e"}, {"id": "27becaa1-07de-31f7-a4ca-934526bc3032", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "430eef03a763e5e76a371ba6d02779ae4a64b6ea <e8f1b0cb9782338c6341ceed816e9c1243743cdd"}, {"id": "93bdc7a5-88d5-33d6-849c-d1b67386b46f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "430eef03a763e5e76a371ba6d02779ae4a64b6ea <7d0b3f745efb24c0aac5e06b49b3420bc65d23b9"}, {"id": "9c977a4f-7081-3a5d-8523-e4619fb7751a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "9f47918d-1dcc-3ff9-89f3-70b3c4b5116c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3"}, {"id": "a2dee57e-ff61-3b50-b1bf-38fdfe14f44d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d7583699-44ad-3944-a919-8bdd7ba2edd6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "daa04da4-57fc-38e4-9c8a-e3074f008b19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "efe33138-0eb8-36a4-ba6c-cd284497ef9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "430eef03a763e5e76a371ba6d02779ae4a64b6ea <776e4e8cbcf155302f430ce9793d1502e3c113a0"}, {"id": "f168cb9d-efcf-35df-9bdc-b9be1cf9471e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d8cc0f20-4c9b-3527-835a-a86e641e6e0b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}